# Lychee ignore patterns (regex, one per line).
# https://github.com/lycheeverse/lychee/blob/master/docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md

# GitHub source links to our own repo — branch-dependent, work on CI/main.
https://github\.com/bastien-gallay/lucid-lint/blob/

# Brainstorm files live in .personal/ (gitignored), never on GitHub.
https://github\.com/bastien-gallay/lucid-lint/blob/main/brainstorm/

# Academic DOIs behind paywalls — 403 ≠ broken.
https://doi\.org/10\.1037/
https://doi\.org/10\.1145/
https://doi\.org/10\.1167/
https://doi\.org/10\.1207/
https://apps\.dtic\.mil/
https://psycnet\.apa\.org/

# EU Publications Office — rate-limited, returns 403 from CI.
https://op\.europa\.eu/

# CDC — bot-blocks the CI runner (403 Forbidden), link resolves in a browser.
https://www\.cdc\.gov/ccindex/

# crates.io — the crate page is a JS SPA whose CDN returns non-2xx to every
# non-browser client (observed 503 from CI, 404/500 from curl), while a real
# browser gets 200. The link is valid — the crate is published (verified via
# `https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/lucid-lint`). This is a deterministic
# bot-block, not a transient blip, so retry cannot fix it → ignore.
https://crates\.io/crates/

# NOTE: transient-flake hosts (vale.sh, cambridge.org/core, scorecard.dev,
# commitmono.com) were removed once the lychee step gained
# `--max-retries 3 --retry-wait-time 2 --timeout 30` (F-lychee-retry). Those
# failures were connection resets / timeouts, which retry absorbs. Only add a
# host back here if it returns a *deterministic* status (403/404) that retry
# cannot fix — otherwise tune the retry/timeout args instead.
